# Notification Types

Create notification events for:

## Warranty Nearing Expiry

Trigger when:

Warranty expires within configurable thresholds:

* 90 days
* 60 days
* 30 days
* 7 days

Notify:

* Customer

Example:

"Your warranty for Samsung Galaxy S24 expires in 30 days."

---

## Missing Documents

Trigger when:

Claim submission lacks required documents.

Examples:

* Receipt missing
* Warranty card missing
* Product image missing
* Diagnostic report missing

Notify:

* Customer

Example:

"Additional documents are required to continue processing Claim CLM-2026-000001."

---

## Claim Submitted

Trigger when:

Customer successfully submits a claim.

Notify:

* Customer

Example:

"Your claim CLM-2026-000001 has been successfully submitted."

---

## Additional Information Requested

Trigger when:

Reviewer requests clarification or more evidence.

Notify:

* Customer

Example:

"A reviewer has requested additional information for Claim CLM-2026-000001."

---

## Claim Moved to Review

Trigger when:

Claim enters manual review.

Notify:

* Customer
* Assigned Reviewer

Example:

"Claim CLM-2026-000001 has been moved to manual review."

---

## Approved Claim

Trigger when:

Claim status changes to APPROVED.

Notify:

* Customer

Example:

"Your claim CLM-2026-000001 has been approved."

---

## Rejected Claim

Trigger when:

Claim status changes to REJECTED.

Notify:

* Customer

Example:

"Your claim CLM-2026-000001 has been rejected."

Include optional rejection reason.

